From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Victor Momplet <mompletvictor@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:53:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(energy): unlogged activity, one active series and priced
 rows for the screens

The day model gains the component the audit found missing once upstream's detector turned out to only
SUGGEST workouts (#2187): a minute outside every window whose mean heart rate reaches resting + 50 % of
the reserve earns its Keytel net above basal, less what its own strap steps already earn (never below
zero), so an unlogged run or ride counts while a brisk walk adds nothing beyond its steps
(UnloggedMinutes; cached per minute as mean bpm + ticks, weight-free). Enters the active energy.

Also: `series()` (the repository's active_kcal points, clamped to the last 120 known days),
`workouts()` composes only the days that have rows, EnergyHooks / EnergyRows for upstream's seams,
`install(app)`; the day's heart rate is read once per stale day (windows are slices of it); `version`
moves only for non-stream changes (a live heart-rate stream would otherwise loop the screens); the
profile's "never filled in" comes from ProfileStore's new flags.

Tests: an unlogged run adds, 105 bpm adds nothing, a minute with steps and a high pulse earns the
larger not the sum, minutes inside a window are left alone; the Robolectric pass covers the resolved
series, priced rows, a meal logged and deleted, a weigh-in that moves its day and the days after only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
